I am a 23 year old male from Mumbai, India.
This is a long post, but I am in great suffering. I have been having really bad headaches for a long time (5+ years) and they have been getting worse. I desperately need help, and even after having done MRI and X-Ray, the doctors couldn't find the problem and the general consensus is I have migraine. I have been given medications like Migarid, Naprosyn, Oxidon, Nervup and Zymoflann. They do relieve my headaches a bit, but my problem is not just limited to headaches.
Every morning, I wake up with a stiff and painful neck. Soon, I will have a bad headache usually localised to one side and in the temporal area, but then spreads throughtout. As the day progresses, the pain gradually spreads all over my upper body, and I can barely move my neck. The place that hurts most are two points on the base of the skull, some points on my neck and the shoulder.
The pain is extreme, and I cannot open my eyes or even sit up. This happens everyday, for more than 5 years. I always have had tinnitus. I have visited the ENT and they confirmed that it was tinnitus (not objective), and had my middle ear checked which came out clear (no problems in middle ear). The static ringing in my ears becomes even louder during my headaches, coupled with a whooshing/sound and pressure; so much that it drowns the outside noise to a great extent.
I also find that I am unable to think clearly. I feel my memory is abysmal, and I cannot study anymore no matter how hard I try. There is too much confusion/issues with concentration. At random points in the day, I have a hot cold feeling, especially during a headache. I cannot tolerate loud noise, light, music, cannot laugh, cry, or get excited, since it induces a terrible headache. My muscles fatigue very quickly, and I feel that I have very high sensitivity to pain.
My neck feels really really stiff, and becomes really painful during a headache. Also, when I have a headache (or when I become excited/anxious), my stomach becomes upset and I pass excessive amounts of gas. I have observed that my muscles get quickly sore when I used to workout. I wake up every morning tired and my neck extremely sore and in pain.
My grades are low, I have trouble remembering things, and at this point, I feel like I have become a "vegetable" that cannot do anything apart from confined to the bed because of the pain. I feel like a very disabled person now. I am becoming more depressed day by day, and I really, really need help urgently.
Here are some of my details-
Age - 23;
Height - 5'8";
Weight - 150 lbs;
Race - Indian;
Habits - Non-smoker, non-alcoholic, rarely drink coffee;
Deficiencies - Had a slight deficiency of Vitamin B12 and Vitamin D earlier;
Sleep - 6-7 hours daily. Sleeping more than that may result in headaches. Taking naps at noon results in headaches. I sleep on my back, since sleeping in any other position guarantees a very sore neck and upper back the next morning and multiple days of continuous headache.
I have visited countless doctors in India regarding my condition. I have had scans and tests which came out clear. I really don't know what else to do know, and would really appreciate if someone has any idea about what is going on.

Mandukaparni / Gotukola / Brahmi*/ Brahmanduki / Asiatic pennywort – Centella asiatica is a herbaceous, frost-tender perennial plant. It is native to the wetlands in Asia. It is used as a culinary vegetable and as a medicinal herb. The hole plant is used in Ayurvedic medicine and cosmetology.
Centella asiatica is indigenous to the Indian subcontinent, Southeast Asia, and wetland regions of the Southeastern US.
It is used in traditional systems of medicine as an antioxidant that rejuvenates and cleanses the body, a tonic for the brain that improves mental activity and memory, strengthens the immune system, improves blood circulation, regulates blood pressure, nervous system, relieves anxiety, heals skin diseases, treats ulcers and scars , strengthens hair and hair follicles, stimulates hair growth, prevents hair loss.
Gotukola is one of the main ingredients of brain tonics. In Ayurveda is called “food for the brain”. Centella A. contains pentacyclic triterpenoids, including asiaticoside, brahmoside, asiuyatic acid, and brahmic acid (madecassic acid). Other constituents include centellose, centelloside, and madecassoside.
Like a tonic for the brain:
– stimulates the brain;
– strengthens memory;
– improves concentration and attention;
– gives clarity of mind;
– nourishes the brain;
– rejuvenates brain cells;
– normalizes cerebral circulation;
– stabilizes the degenerative cognitive function of older adults on attention, memory, function of the musculoskeletal system and reaction time;
– helps treat atherosclerosis, Alzheimer’s disease;
– increases efficiency, learning ability, improves short-term and long-term memory, treats amnesia;
– expands the cognitive abilities of healthy people, activates their mental activity, the ability to remember and reproduce information;
– protects the blood vessels through which oxygen enters the brain, thereby stimulating the flow of oxygen to the brain.
As a tonic for the nervous system:
– relieves anxiety, stress, tension, helps with depression, including postpartum depression;
– gives a feeling of calm and relaxation, while simultaneously activating mental processes;
– normalizes sleep, treats insomnia (tea from Gotu Kola is taken before bedtime for a healthy sleep and quick wake up).
As a treatment for many skin diseases:
– has an anti-inflammatory effect, strengthens blood vessels and capillaries, which supply blood to the tissues of the affected areas, improving blood circulation and stimulating blood flow, thereby contributing to the rapid healing of wounds;
– applying an extract of gotu kola to the skin might help reduce keloids; taking gotu kola by mouth may improve the appearance of keloid;
– the cream containing gotukola and other ingredients may help prevent stretch marks during pregnancy;
– applying a specific gotu kola cream to the skin twice daily for 6-8 weeks after the removal of stitches might help reduce scarring.
– varicose veins and chronic venous insufficiency (strengthens vascular tissue);
– might help prevent blood clots that form in the veins (venous thromboembolism or VTE)
– scleroderma (a disease in which tissue compaction occurs);
– for the diabetic microangiopathy: might help increase circulation and decrease fluid retention in people with diabetes whose small blood vessels have been damaged by their disease;
– hardening of the arteries (atherosclerosis);
– cleanse the blood;
– improve blood circulation;
– like a tonic for the whole body;
– common cold and flu; Tonsillitis;
– other conditions.
Don’t use gotu kola if you are: pregnant, breastfeeding, have hepatitis or other liver disease, have a scheduled surgery within the next two weeks, under 18 years of age, have a history of skin cancer.
Consult your doctor before use if you: have liver disease, have diabetes, have high cholesterol, are taking medications such as sedatives for sleep or anxiety, are taking diuretics.
Additional informaion: Gotu Kola (Centella asiatica) is often confused with another plant – Brahmi (Bacopa monnieri). Both plants are called brahmi because in Ayurveda, the name “brahmi” can be applied to any powerful tonic for the brain, given that it carries the energy of the god Brahma, the creator of the universe in Hinduism. However, it so happened that the word “brahmi” most often refers to bacopa monnieri. Brahmi and Gotu Kola are the most powerful brain tonics in Ayurveda. These two plants are extremely similar to each other in appearance and properties. Both are used in Ayurveda as the two most powerful tonics for the brain, in cosmetic formulas for face and body skin, and especially for hair.
These two plants are perfectly combined with each other. Both are powerful antioxidants that cleanse the blood, strengthen the immune system, tone the entire body, treat a number of diseases, including skin diseases, and also perfectly heal wounds and ulcers. However, Brahmi has a cooling effect that regulates vata and kapha dosha, and Gotu-kola has a warming effect that normalizes pitta dosha. Thus, together they perfectly balance all three doshas, the whole organism. Both herbs are taken orally as a medicine and are part of numerous cosmetic preparations. Brahmi is more used for food additives and face and body skin care products, and Gotu Kola is used in cosmetics for face and hair (this is a very conditional difference).

Neuralgia of the back – a condition that causes severe pain. It occurs against the background of damage to peripheral nerve fibers. This disease occurs quite often, it can occur in both adults and children.
The cause of extreme discomfort is compression of the nerves with inflamed tissues. Pathological changes affect the narrow interosseous spaces between the ribs. Patients have been trying for some time to get rid of the disease at home, because of which they start its course until serious complications appear. You should not take painkillers for a long time, it is best to consult your doctor as soon as possible.
Causes of appearance
A huge number of factors can provoke the appearance of painful sensations caused by back neuralgia.
Doctors refer to the immediate causes of this pathology:
- Serious diseases of the nervous system – people who often experience neuralgia should be checked regularly by a neurologist. Typically, this condition occurs in those who are at increased risk of multiple sclerosis;
- Infectious processes – pathogenic microorganisms have an extremely negative effect on the state of the body, they are able to aggravate the course of this disease. The greatest danger is influenza, lichen and tuberculosis. Even the common cold, in which a person did not receive treatment in a timely manner, can lead to similar consequences;
- The use of certain drugs. Back neuralgia can occur as a side effect of prolonged use of a number of medications. Chemical components during reactions can release toxic compounds that adversely affect the state of the body;
- Injuries. If the back is damaged, nerve injury may occur. This is the most common cause of neuralgia in children;
- The presence of tumors. Neoplasms in the spine or ribs can provoke damage to nerve fibers, because of which a person is forced to suffer from discomfort.
Diagnosing neuralgia of the back is quite simple. The patient goes to the doctor with complaints of severe dull lower back pain. It is there that the blocked nerve is located. In rare cases, patients characterize the pain as paroxysmal, subsiding from time to time.
In this case, secondary signs of the pain syndrome are observed: increased sweating, high body temperature, pallor of the skin and trembling in the muscles throughout the body.
In the initial stages, neuralgia of the back develops with a sharp muscle spasm, which occurs against the background of a sharp movement. Most often, patients begin to feel discomfort after sleeping in an uncomfortable position, weight lifting, back injury.
Another feature of back neuralgia is a strong pain syndrome during palpation of the back spine. It also occurs during manipulations with the sides of the thoracic spine. The greatest discomfort is manifested in the intercostal zone.
What happens if you ignore neuralgia?
With neuralgia of the back, the muscles responsible for the extension of the spinal column are affected. If untreated, all discs located from the shoulder blades to the lower back undergo a degenerative process. A person experiences severe pain.
If treatment is not started in time, the patient may experience serious complications.
First of all, he has specular pains radiating to his arms and legs. Over time, an atrophy of the abdominal muscles is formed, because of which a person becomes constrained in his movements.
The muscles of the respiratory apparatus are also disrupted – they become weak, a person cannot fully breathe. Over time, he develops signs of shingles, herpes – any watery vesicles on the surface of the skin. It is accompanied by all the increased body temperature, additionally there are changes in the chemical composition of the blood.
With prolonged absence of treatment, pain from back neuralgia recedes. Despite this, in the future, a person faces serious relapses: inflammation increases, soreness fetters the whole body. The patient cannot move.
If you do not provide him with full medical support, there is a risk of developing paralysis.
If you consult a doctor in the initial stages of the course of this disease, you can get rid of the painful sensations quite quickly. It is strictly forbidden to engage in home self-medication, as this can lead to serious complications.
First of all, it is necessary to do everything possible to stop the pain syndrome. To do this, the specialist needs to determine exactly what triggered the neuralgia.
To successfully get rid of soreness, the following methods are used:
- Drug therapy;
- Manual therapy;
- Physiotherapeutic procedures;
- Therapeutic physical training.
Physiotherapeutic procedures are also recommended for the prevention of neuralgia in the future. Try to do herbal baths, warm-ups, or ultrasounds from time to time. This favorably affects the state of muscle fibers, prevents spasms.
However, before you go to the doctor, you must always consult with a specialist.
The basis of the treatment of neuralgia of the back is the use of medications. They are aimed at reducing soreness, getting rid of the inflammatory process, as well as restoring the functionality of damaged tissues.
Keep in mind that prescribing drugs should be exclusively by the attending physician based on a detailed diagnosis.
The following medicines are usually used:
- Anti-inflammatory and analgesic drugs – Ibuprofen, Ortofen, Naproxen, Diclofenac;
- To relieve muscle spasm – Gabapentin, Carbamazepine, Finlepsin;
- Antidepressants to restore muscle tone – Duloxetine, Amitriptyline;
- To normalize blood circulation – B vitamins;
- For the relief of pain – novocaine blockade;
- To relieve puffiness – Voltaren, Finalgon, Diclofenac, Indomethacin.
Traditional methods of treatment
It is possible to get rid of neuralgia of the back without drug therapy, however, for this to begin treatment is necessary in the initial stages of this disease.
